  "title": "Ziyarat of the Daughters of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)",
  "data": "At the graves of the Prophet's daughters in al-Baqi, recite, in hope of its reward:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA RASOOLA RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Messenger of the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفْوَةَ جَمِيْعِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFWATA JAMEE'IL ANBIYAA'I WAL MURSALEEN\nPeace be upon you, O choicest of all the prophets and messengers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنِ اخْتَارَهُ اللّٰهُ عَلَى الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MANIKH TAARAHULLAAHU A'LAL KHALQI AJMA'EENA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O you whom Allah chose above all creation, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى بَنَاتِ السَّيِّدِ الْمُصْطَفٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA BANAATIS SAYYIDIL MUSTAFAA\nPeace be upon the daughters of the chosen master.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى بَنَاتِ النَّبِيِّ الْمُجْتَبٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA BANAATIN NABIYYIL MUJTABAA\nPeace be upon the daughters of the elect Prophet.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى بَنَاتِ مَنِ اصْطَفَاهُ اللّٰهُ فِي السَّمَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA BANAATI MANIS TAFAAHULLAAHU FIS SAMAA'\nPeace be upon the daughters of him whom Allah chose in heaven\nوَفَضَّلَهٗ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ الْبَرِيَّةِ وَالْوَرٰى\nWA FADDALAHOO A'LAA JAMEE'IL BARIYYATI WAL WARAA\nand favoured above all creation and all people.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى ذُرِّيَّةِ السَّيِّدِ الْجَلِيْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA DHURRIYYATIS SAYYIDIL JALEEL\nPeace be upon the offspring of the majestic master,\nمِنْ نَسْلِ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ وَسُلَالَةِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ الْخَلِيْلِ\nMIN NASLI ISMAA'EELA WA SULAALATI IBRAAHEEMAL KHALEEL\nof the line of Isma'il and the lineage of Ibrahim, the Friend (of Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى بَنَاتِ النَّبِيِّ الرَّسُوْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA BANAATIN NABIYYIR RASOOL\nPeace be upon the daughters of the Prophet and Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَخَوَاتِ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ الْبَتُوْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA AKHAWAATI FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'IL BATOOL\nPeace be upon the sisters of Fatimah al-Zahra, the Pure.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الذُّرِّيَّةِ الطَّيِّبَةِ الطَّاهِرَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LADH DHURRIYYATIT TAYYIBATIT TAAHIRAH\nPeace be upon the good and pure offspring\nوَالْعِتْرَةِ الزَّاكِيَةِ الزَّاهِرَةِ بَنَاتِ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nWAL I'TRATIZ ZAAKIYATIZ ZAAHIRATI BANAATI KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nand the chaste and radiant family, the daughters of the Seal of the Prophets,\nوَسَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nWA SAYYIDIL ANBIYAA'I WAL MURSALEEN\nthe master of the prophets and messengers,\nوَخِيَرَةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA KHIYARATI RASOOLILLAAHI AJMA'EEN\nand the chosen of the Messenger of Allah, all of them.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الذُّرِّيَّةِ الطَّاهِرَةِ الزَّاكِيَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LADH DHURRIYYATIT TAAHIRATIZ ZAAKIYAH\nPeace be upon the pure and chaste offspring\nوَالْعِتْرَةِ الْمُصْطَفَوِيَّةِ\nWAL I'TRATIL MUSTAFAWIYYAH\nand the family of the Chosen One.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى زَيْنَبَ وَاُمِّ كُلْثُوْمٍ وَرُقَيَّةَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ZAYNABA WA UMMI KULTHOOMIN WA RUQAYYAH\nPeace be upon Zainab, Umm Kulthum and Ruqayyah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الشَّرِيْفَاتِ الْاَحْسَابِ وَالطَّاهِرَاتِ الْاَنْسَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LASH SHAREEFAATIL AHSAABI WAT TAAHIRAATIL ANSAAB\nPeace be upon the ladies of noble descent and pure lineage.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى بَنَاتِ الْاٰبَاۤءِ الْاَعَاظِمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA BANAATIL AABAA'IL A'AAZIM\nPeace be upon the daughters of the great forefathers\nوَسُلَالَةِ الْاَجْدَادِ الْاَكَارِمِ الْاَفَاخِمِ\nWA SULAALATIL AJDAADIL AKAARIMIL AFAAKHIM\nand the lineage of the noble and illustrious ancestors,\nعَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ وَعَبْدِ مَنَافٍ وَهَاشِمٍ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nA'BDIL MUTTALIBI WA A'BDI MANAAFIN WA HAASHIMIN WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAbd al-Muttalib, Abd Manaf and Hashim; and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "By the common account the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) had four daughters by Lady Khadijah (s.a.): Zainab, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum and Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (s.a.). Some Shia scholars hold that Zainab, Ruqayyah and Umm Kulthum were daughters of Lady Khadijah's sister, brought up in the Prophet's house, and that Lady Fatimah (s.a.) was his only daughter. The three died in Madinah in the Prophet's lifetime and were buried in al-Baqi.\n\nThis ziyarat is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, without a narrated source, to be recited in hope of its reward (raja')."
